From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Really Board Support <build@really.local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: really: enable SDMMC power domain before U-Boot proper

The RK3588 PMU is protected from the non-secure U-Boot proper runtime.
Assert the PD_SDMMC power request while SPL still runs in the privileged
pre-ATF context, so U-Boot proper can initialize the microSD controller.

---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
@@ -221,6 +221,10 @@
 
 void spl_board_prepare_for_boot(void)
 {
+	u32 val = readl((void *)0xfd8d8150);
+
+	writel(val | 0x2000, (void *)0xfd8d8150);
+	dsb();
 	really_spl_log_marker();
 
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARM64) || CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SYS_DCACHE_OFF))
-- 
2.43.0
